[%out 4236] [%in 2] [%cacheread 0] [%cachewrite 1879] Red's knight on d4 is
attacking my pawn on e6. Right now nothing protects that pawn, so Red could
simply win it with 马六进五. I'll play 马8进7 (h9g7). The knight's leg point h8
is empty, so the move is legal. It does four things: - **Guards e6.** The
knight on g7 covers e6, so if Red takes with 马六进五, I recapture and Red
loses a knight for a pawn. - **Attacks Red's cannon.** The g7 knight hits the
cannon on h5 (leg point g6 is empty), so Red has to deal with it. - **Takes the
knight out of the cannon's line.** Red's cannon on h5 could jump over my cannon
on h7 and capture on h9. Once the knight leaves, that target is gone. -
**Covers f5.** If Red plays 马六进四 to f5, I can take it with the g7 knight.
At worst the knights get traded. Pushing the e-pawn instead (e6e5) doesn't
work. Red's cannon on h5 would jump over my pawn on g5 and take it on e5. } 8.
