[%emt 0:02:30] [%think 13813] [%out 14290] [%in 2] [%cacheread 0]
[%cachewrite 2166] The d8 车 goes to d5 (车4进3). This removes the threat from
马d4 and attacks the 炮 on b5. **What 红方 was threatening:** Moving the 炮
from d5 to b5 opened the d-file. If the 马 on d4 then jumps to c6, it attacks
my 车 on d8 twice: once from the 马 and once from the 车 on d2 behind it. **Why
d5:** - The 车 on d5 blocks the 马's legs. 马d4 can no longer go to c6 or e6,
so the fork is gone and the e6 卒 is safe. - The 车 on d5 attacks the 炮 on b5
along row 5, and nothing protects b5. - d5 itself is safe. The 车 on d2 is
blocked by its own 马, and the 炮 on b5 has no screen. **If the 马 moves off d4
to open the 车 on d2:** - 马d4-f5: I trade 车 with d5xd2, and after 仕e1xd2 my
马 takes f5 with g7xf5. I win a 马. - 马 to f3, c2 or e2: I take the 炮 with
d5xb5. - 炮b5xg5 (jumping over d5): my 象 recaptures with e7xg5. 红方 loses a
炮 for a 卒. So 红方 basically has to retreat the 炮, and my 车 has a good
active post. } 19. 相七退五 炮２平４ { [%emt 0:01:33] [%think 7986] [%out 8239]
