车二平一 炮９平７ { [%emt 0:03:23] [%think 19081] [%out 19448] [%in 2]
[%cacheread 0] [%cachewrite 2525] Red's rook on i1 attacks my cannon on i4. The
cannon has to move, so I want a square that also creates a threat. - **The
move:** move the cannon to g4, where my horse on g6 acts as the screen. The
cannon then attacks Red's pawn on g8. - **Why that pawn matters:** the g8 pawn
is the only thing protecting Red's cannon on h8. My rook on h9 and horse on g6
both attack that cannon. - **If Red retreats the cannon:** I take the pawn with
炮×g8 and gain a pawn. - **If Red moves the pawn away:** the cannon on h8 has
no protection, and my rook or horse wins it. - **If Red plays 车×i6, attacking
my horse:** I can play 马×h8 or 炮×g8. Either way the exchanges come out
roughly even, so I am not worse. - **Other squares:** f4 and h4 are covered by
Red's horse, and e4 is covered by the pawn on e3. The remaining safe squares on
the left carry no threat, so g4 is the best of the options. } 34. 相五进三
